  "term": "mesolimbic system",
  "definition": "The mesolimbic system is a major dopamine pathway in the brain that links the midbrain with the limbic system. It runs from the ventral tegmental area to the nucleus accumbens and also connects with areas including the amygdala and prefrontal cortex.",
